# Reference ONLY - variable names and shapes, never real values.
#
# ==========================================================================
# DO NOT PUT PRODUCTION SETTINGS IN backend/.env
# ==========================================================================
#
# server.py calls load_dotenv(backend/.env) at import. Anything in that file
# is therefore picked up by EVERY local process that imports the backend -
# including the whole test suite. Putting APP_ENV=production and a real
# Supabase DATABASE_URL there does two bad things at once:
#
#   1. it points local development and local tests at the REAL production
#      database, where a test run can do destructive things to live data;
#   2. it breaks ~250 tests immediately, because the shared engine becomes
#      PostgreSQL and db.DB_PATH (a SQLite-only concept) becomes None.
#
# (backend/tests/conftest.py now defends against exactly this, but the
# defence only covers the test suite - not a dev server you start by hand.)
#
# Production configuration does NOT live in a .env file at all. It lives in:
#
#   %LOCALAPPDATA%\EchoCast-AI\persistent-lan-server\keys\database-url.txt
#
# read once at HQ start by tools/hq_runtime.py and passed to the backend
# through its process environment only. See
# docs/SUPABASE_PRODUCTION_CUTOVER.md for the exact steps.
#
# ==========================================================================
# What the two variables mean
# ==========================================================================

# Unset (or anything other than 'production') = development: local SQLite,
# no DATABASE_URL needed, no internet connection required. This is the
# correct value for a developer machine, and the only correct value for a
# backend/.env file.
APP_ENV=development

# Required ONLY when APP_ENV=production, and supplied there by
# keys/database-url.txt rather than by this file. Shown here purely to
# document the expected shape - a Supabase "Session Pooler" (Supavisor,
# port 5432) string, NOT the Direct Connection and NOT the Transaction
# Pooler on 6543. Never paste a real password into any file under Git.
#
#   postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
